in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @loss

# @mirror/loss — the substrate's loss family root at the mirror altitude.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-07, Alex → Mara): the substrate already
# has loss declared at three altitudes — `type loss = pure - real`
# (boot/01-meta.mirror; the algebraic floor), `grammar @loss` with
# `type measurement = shannon | fiedler | cheeger | entropy | mixing`
# (boot/01a-error.mirror; the measurement enumeration), and
# `transparency(p)` as the substrate's loss carrier (glass.mirror;
# the located-opacity carrier with success / partial / failure
# constructors). The family root lifts these from grammar-altitude
# declarations to the mirror altitude where sub-glasses parameterize
# the `L: Loss` slot on `imperfect<a, e, l>` as typed species under
# one named family. The same lift that gave us `@cli → @mirror/lens/cli`
# (the 2026-06-06 lens family migration); the same lift that gave us
# `@mirror/spec` (the project manifold grammar).
#
# Load-bearing recognition: **glass and lens are two names for one
# primitive at three altitudes.** Glass at the substrate-declaration
# altitude carries typed surfaces with properties and restriction
# maps (`shards/glass.mirror`'s `glass(name) -> prism { \ }`
# keyword; `splinter`, `shard`, `transparency`, `verdict` as the
# floor declarations). Lens at the optics-implementation altitude
# carries the observation/projection family with the same five-
# operation algebra rendered through a typed surface
# (`shards/mirror/lens.mirror`'s `prism @mirror/lens { ... }` family
# root; cli / shell / mcp / lsp / transit / refract as species).
# Restriction map at the sheaf-theoretic altitude carries section
# gluing (the conductivity tensor's edge maps per
# `epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.mirror`; the cellular sheaf's
# Čech complex per the eigensheaf spec). These are the same
# primitive at three altitudes — a typed-surface-with-restriction-
# maps that carries data from one altitude into another while
# preserving the algebra. The substrate's `glass <name>` declaration
# IS a `lens <name>` declaration IS a restriction-map declaration.
#
# The 23rd-instance substrate-pull recognition: every "missing
# concept" turns out to be a name the substrate was already
# implicitly using. Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]:
# 22 prior instances logged; this is the 23rd. The substrate has
# been using `glass` (declaration altitude), `lens` (observation
# altitude), `restriction map` (sheaf altitude), `splinter.lens`
# (the referring-splinter shape per glass.mirror's splinter_shape
# enum) consistently; the collapse is recognition-level, not
# keyword-level. The names stay where they are. The recognition
# names that they're the same primitive.
#
# Why this matters for the loss family: each sub-glass under
# `@mirror/loss/` IS a lens INTO the loss algebra. The lens projects
# the substrate's running state into a measurement (a scalar; a
# located opacity map; a higher-arity Massey class); the
# measurement composes back through the imperfect functor's `L`
# slot; the substrate's transparency monoid (Fail-dominates /
# Partial-min-confidence / Pass-neutral per
# `glass.mirror`'s transparency declaration) composes the sub-
# glasses' losses into the parent's verdict. Each `glass
# @mirror/loss/<name>` IS a lens into the substrate's loss space
# at that name's altitude.
#
# === Discipline ===
#
# A `@mirror/loss` instance IS:
#
#   - a typed-surface-with-restriction-map: same five-operation
#     algebra, different L (loss carrier) chosen at the sub-glass
#     altitude. The runtime evaluates the same algebra; each
#     sub-glass parameterizes the imperfect functor's loss slot
#     for a specific measurement shape (located opacity map for
#     transparency; scalar bits for shannon; Dirichlet energy for
#     dirichlet; H² Massey class for massey).
#   - a projection INTO the loss algebra, not a parallel one:
#     sub-glasses do not OWN loss state. The loss state lives on
#     the substrate's running imperfect carriers; each sub-glass
#     reads through to the same carrier through the same monoid.
#     Two sub-glasses observing the same imperfect MUST see the
#     same total transparency under the projection; divergence is
#     a bug by construction (the lens discipline per
#     `shards/mirror/lens.mirror`).
#   - composable under the Transparency monoid: sub-glass losses
#     compose under the existing `Transparency<P>` monoid declared
#     at the glass floor (per `glass.mirror`'s transparency type).
#     No parallel combine; the algebra is borrowed verbatim from
#     the substrate floor.
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
# All four sub-glasses correspond to measurement variants the
# substrate already enumerates in `boot/01a-error.mirror`'s
# `type measurement = shannon | fiedler | cheeger | entropy | mixing`,
# plus the higher-arity Massey class derived from the prophecy
# insight (2026-06-07).
#
# Carrier sub-glasses:
#
#   @mirror/loss/transparency  the canonical carrier per `glass.mirror`.
#                              `transparency<p>` over a property `p`;
#                              success / partial(opacity_map) /
#                              failure(opacity_map). Fail-dominates /
#                              Partial-min-confidence / Pass-neutral
#                              algebra. The substrate's primary loss
#                              vocabulary; what every other sub-glass
#                              lifts into when composing into the
#                              parent imperfect's L slot. Landed this
#                              tick (substrate-pull-lift from
#                              glass.mirror's floor declaration).
#
# Scalar sub-glass (forward-promise):
#
#   @mirror/loss/shannon       the scalar information-theoretic loss
#                              per `boot/01a-error.mirror`'s
#                              measurement = shannon enumeration. Bits
#                              of missing information; composes additively;
#                              the Imperfect monad's L = f64 instance.
#                              `glass.mirror`'s opacity.weight field is
#                              already shannon-shaped ("bits-of-missing-
#                              information at this site (Shannon-like)");
#                              this sub-glass lifts that floor field
#                              into a typed measurement at the mirror
#                              altitude. Forward-promised; lands when
#                              a consumer pulls a scalar L parameter.
#
# Energy sub-glass (forward-promise):
#
#   @mirror/loss/dirichlet     the sheaf Dirichlet energy `½⟨x, Δ₀x⟩`
#                              per T8 / T9's sheaf Laplacian. Per
#                              `epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.mirror`'s
#                              `λ₀(Δ_F)` computation; per Bodnar 2022's
#                              Neural Sheaf Diffusion gradient flow
#                              to `ker(Δ_0) = H⁰(F)`. The kintsugi
#                              loop's gradient flow descends this
#                              functional; eⁿ⁺¹ < eⁿ is
#                              Polyak-Łojasiewicz on this energy.
#                              Forward-promised; lands when the
#                              sheaf-diffusion Houdini fixpoint pulls.
#
# Higher-arity sub-glass (forward-promise):
#
#   @mirror/loss/massey        the noncommutative-curvature carrier
#                              per Markl 2024 (arXiv:2404.19607). The
#                              `conundrum` IS non-vanishing Massey
#                              product `⟨α,β,γ⟩ ∈ H²`; per Markl's
#                              Remark 10 the Massey cocycle is
#                              `c(D) = -dD + D·D`, noncommutative
#                              curvature of the connection D. A
#                              substrate is formal iff it has no
#                              conundra (DGMS 1975). Per the prophecy
#                              insight (2026-06-07): pairs with
#                              `@mirror/homotopy/massey` as the
#                              constructive-derivation sub-shard.
#                              Forward-promised; lands when the
#                              homotopy/A_infinity pull comes through.
#
# === Why one family ===
#
# All four sub-glasses parameterize the same `L` slot on
# `imperfect<a, e, l>` declared at the glass floor. Without the
# family, every consumer (kintsugi loop; sheaf-diffusion fixpoint;
# conundrum detector) lands its loss carrier at an ad-hoc altitude
# (`@bits`, `@energy`, `@curvature`, `@h2`) and the cross-cutting
# discipline (Transparency-monoid composition; imperfect's L-slot;
# the lens projection into the substrate's running state) has to
# be re-justified per measurement. With the family, the discipline
# IS the family. The 22 prior substrate-pull recognitions
# established the rhythm; this one runs the same play at the
# measurement altitude.
#
# === Sibling relationship to @mirror/lens ===
#
# `@mirror/lens` observes the substrate's running state through
# typed transport surfaces (cli / shell / mcp / lsp) and measurement-
# shape surfaces (transit / refract). `@mirror/loss` observes the
# substrate's running loss algebra through typed measurement
# carriers (transparency / shannon / dirichlet / massey). Per the
# glass-IS-lens recognition above: these are sibling families at
# the mirror altitude, not parent-child. Both project the same
# five-operation algebra through their own typed surfaces; both
# compose under the same Transparency<P> monoid; both observe state
# without owning it. `@mirror/spectral` (the agent coordination
# layer) consumes both — the conductor reads refract (a lens species);
# the audition reads pending morphisms ranked by their losses (the
# loss family's species). The dependency points downstream from the
# family roots; the roots stay decoupled.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Every type and action below names an established object older
# than the discipline of computer science (modulo discipline names):
#
#   loss            Wiener (1948), Cybernetics; the residual
#                    between predicted and observed in a feedback
#                    loop. The substrate's reading is
#                    boot/01-meta.mirror's `loss = pure - real`
#                    — the algebraic floor lifted by Wiener.
#   measurement     Bridgman (1927), The Logic of Modern Physics;
#                    operationalism. The measurement IS the
#                    operation that produces the number. The
#                    substrate's reading is
#                    boot/01a-error.mirror's measurement variants
#                    — each variant IS one operation that produces
#                    one shape of loss number.
#   transparency    Hayek (1945), The Use of Knowledge in Society;
#                    the located, partial, contextual knowledge that
#                    cannot be centralized. The substrate's reading
#                    is glass.mirror's `transparency<p>` carrier with
#                    opacity_map naming WHERE the partiality lives.
#   lens            Bartlett (1932), Remembering; the schema as
#                    selective surface that constructs what's seen.
#                    The substrate's reading is
#                    shards/mirror/lens.mirror's family-altitude
#                    declaration. Per the collapse above: also the
#                    same primitive as the splinter.lens shape
#                    (cross-altitude link) and the sheaf restriction
#                    map (section gluing).
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: `prism
# @mirror/loss { ... }` declares the family IS a prism. The
# five-operation block below is the canonical declaration form
# (cf. shards/mirror/lens.mirror, shards/mirror/spectral.mirror,
# shards/mirror/spec.mirror). Each sub-glass specialises from there.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/transparency.md (the floor transparency
#               declaration this family lifts),
#               docs/specs/eigensheaf.md (the Dirichlet-energy
#               descent that @mirror/loss/dirichlet parameterizes),
#               docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md (the imperfect-
#               as-monad floor with L slot),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-07-prophecy-derived-fractures-
#               from-topology.md (Markl 2024 Massey-as-A_∞ ground
#               for @mirror/loss/massey; the four-sub-shard cascade
#               this family root sits sibling to).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (the same lift that gave @cli → @mirror/lens/cli;
#                      grammar-altitude @loss → mirror-altitude
#                      @mirror/loss),
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (transparency and imperfect are substrate
#                      vocabulary; this family lifts them into typed
#                      species),
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the loss
#                      carriers ascend the bounded semilattice;
#                      kintsugi's eⁿ⁺¹ < eⁿ IS the monotone descent
#                      of the chosen L's distance to ker(Δ₀)),
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (the
#                      L slot's choice IS the D component of (A, H,
#                      D); the family parameterizes which Dirac the
#                      substrate runs).
# Substrate recognitions: [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the 23rd-instance: @loss grammar already
#                      named the five measurement variants;
#                      transparency floor already named the carrier;
#                      this family lifts what was already there),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (the family root
#                      pulls loss from grammar floor to mirror
#                      altitude; no invention, only lift),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (at every Fate-tournament altitude, the loss
#                      is a composite of @epistemologic/properties;
#                      sub-glasses are the composition surface).
# Forward-promise to consumers:
#   - @mirror/loss/shannon  lands when a consumer pulls a scalar L
#                            parameter (the bits-of-missing-information
#                            measurement; trivially additive monoid).
#   - @mirror/loss/dirichlet lands when the sheaf-diffusion Houdini
#                             fixpoint pulls (per the eigensheaf spec;
#                             per Bodnar 2022's NSD).
#   - @mirror/loss/massey   lands when @mirror/homotopy/massey pulls
#                            (per the prophecy insight's cascade order;
#                            the constructive H² derivation per Markl
#                            Lemma 14).
#   - The @mirror/store/crystal pull (next-in-cascade per the
#                            prophecy insight) reads `transparency`
#                            as the verdict payload carrier; this
#                            family root + transparency sub-glass
#                            unblock that pull.
# Related shards: glass.mirror (transparency and imperfect floor;
#                 the L slot this family parameterizes),
#                 boot/01a-error.mirror (the @loss grammar this
#                 family lifts; the measurement enumeration this
#                 family realises sub-glass by sub-glass),
#                 boot/01-meta.mirror (the algebraic floor
#                 `loss = pure - real`),
#                 mirror/lens.mirror (the sibling family; observation
#                 to loss's measurement; glass-IS-lens recognition
#                 makes the sibling structural),
#                 mirror/spectral.mirror (the consumer family; the
#                 audition reads pending morphisms ranked by their
#                 sub-glass losses),
#                 mirror/spectral/score.mirror (the eigenboard context
#                 carrier; its pending field's morphisms carry sub-
#                 glass losses for the SDRF ranking),
#                 epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.mirror (the
#                 λ₀(Δ_F) computation @mirror/loss/dirichlet will
#                 parameterize when it lands),
#                 epistemologic/math/curvature.mirror (the Balanced
#                 Forman ranking; consumer of dirichlet sub-glass
#                 outputs).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/loss.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/loss` as the family root; sub-glasses live at
# `shards/mirror/loss/<name>.mirror`.

prism @mirror/loss {
  focus loss
  project loss
  split loss
  shift loss
  settle loss
}

out @mirror/loss
